E712 [*] Avoid equality comparisons to `True` or `False`
 --> E711_E712_basedpython.by:6:11
  |
4 |     print(b < a == None)  # E711
5 |     print(b < a != None)  # E711
6 |     print(b == c == False)  # E712
  |           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
7 |     print(a == None == b)  # E711
  |
help: Replace comparison
  |
5 |     print(b < a != None)  # E711
  -     print(b == c == False)  # E712
6 +     print(b == c === False)  # E712
7 |     print(a == None == b)  # E711
  |
note: This is an unsafe fix and may change runtime behavior

E712 [*] Avoid equality comparisons to `True`; use `c:` for truth checks
  --> E711_E712_basedpython.by:14:11
   |
12 |     print(a == None)  # E711
13 |     print(a != None)  # E711
14 |     print(c == True)  # E712
   |           ^^^^^^^^^
help: Replace with `c`
   |
13 |     print(a != None)  # E711
   -     print(c == True)  # E712
14 +     print(c)  # E712
   |
note: This is an unsafe fix and may change runtime behavior
